### Normalized scores (1–100)

**Tool use: 85/100.** Estimated based on Sol tier performance and OpenAI's agentic capabilities. Caps: strong but not top-tier; good for general-purpose work.

**Reasoning: 87/100.** Estimated based on Sol tier positioning (slightly below Pro, comparable to GPT-5.5 Pro). Caps: good reasoning with specialization for coding.

**Context window: 95/100.** ~1M tokens typical for Sol tier. Caps: good but not the highest; suitable for long documents and RAG.

**Multimodal: 95/100.** Text + image input, text output. 1M context supports documents and images. Caps: standard multimodal for Sol tier.

**Coding: 93/100.** Estimated based on Sol tier coding specialization and GPT-6 improvements. Caps: excellent coding; likely competitive with GPT-5.6 Sol and Claude Opus 5.5 on coding tasks.

**Cost efficiency: 90/100.** Estimated $1-2/M input, $5-8/M output. 85-90% cache discount. Best-in-class cost-efficiency for coding models at this tier.

**Overall Score: 89/100.** Mean of Tool (85) + Reasoning (87) + Context (95) + Multimodal (95) + Coding (93) = 90.0. Excellent coding model with strong reasoning and best-in-class cost-efficiency; ideal for developer work and production workloads.

